WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:02.397
The summer shutdown is over.

2
00:00:03.123 --> 00:00:05.457
Line 3 now runs in hall B.

3
00:00:06.429 --> 00:00:08.937
The work is done, but the project is not.

4
00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:13.474
The goal was line 3 in hall B, as fast as before.

5
00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:15.120
Has it been met?

6
00:00:16.162 --> 00:00:19.645
We follow this one project through the four topics of the module.

7
00:00:20.347 --> 00:00:22.890
The details come later, in the lessons.

8
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.477
The first topic is Proving results.

9
00:00:27.185 --> 00:00:28.276
Did it really work?

10
00:00:29.311 --> 00:00:31.471
Does line 3 still run as fast?

11
00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:35.834
Then you measure in exactly the same way as before the move.

12
00:00:36.863 --> 00:00:38.639
One good week proves nothing.

13
00:00:39.384 --> 00:00:42.334
Every week varies a little, even without the move.

14
00:00:43.105 --> 00:00:43.987
That is noise.

15
00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:48.927
For proving results we often use a baseline and a run chart.

16
00:00:50.303 --> 00:00:52.811
The second topic is Handover and closure.

17
00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.830
When is the project done?

18
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:58.979
The sponsor goes through the list you agreed at the start.

19
00:00:59.744 --> 00:01:00.835
All of it is met.

20
00:01:01.646 --> 00:01:04.816
Then comes the sign-off, the sponsor’s formal yes.

21
00:01:05.838 --> 00:01:09.321
One point stays open, because line 4 comes later.

22
00:01:10.047 --> 00:01:12.265
It goes on the open points list.

23
00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:17.108
The team lead is the owner, because he stays when the project is gone.

24
00:01:18.181 --> 00:01:19.354
Then you close down.

25
00:01:20.091 --> 00:01:25.060
The time code is closed, the final invoice goes out and access is revoked.

26
00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:27.978
Otherwise people keep booking hours.

27
00:01:28.974 --> 00:01:34.210
For handover and closure we often use acceptance criteria and a close-out checklist.

28
00:01:35.542 --> 00:01:38.677
The third topic is Retrospective and lessons learned.

29
00:01:39.441 --> 00:01:41.554
What do we take to the next project?

30
00:01:42.589 --> 00:01:45.445
The team looks back, the people on the line too.

31
00:01:46.144 --> 00:01:49.325
What do we repeat, and what do we do differently next time?

32
00:01:50.077 --> 00:01:51.563
That is a retrospective.

33
00:01:52.586 --> 00:01:56.359
Talking about what went wrong only works when it feels safe.

34
00:01:57.062 --> 00:01:59.210
That is called psychological safety.

35
00:02:00.236 --> 00:02:03.393
A lesson becomes an action, with an owner and a moment.

36
00:02:04.137 --> 00:02:05.611
The switchboard came late.

37
00:02:06.363 --> 00:02:10.241
So at the next start the buyer asks for a fixed delivery date.

38
00:02:11.292 --> 00:02:15.855
For retrospective and lessons we often use a timeline and a lessons report.

39
00:02:17.216 --> 00:02:20.478
The fourth topic is Client relationship and follow-up.

40
00:02:21.204 --> 00:02:22.992
How do you leave the client stronger?

41
00:02:23.995 --> 00:02:26.062
The closing report is one page.

42
00:02:26.771 --> 00:02:29.372
Answer first, the evidence is below it.

43
00:02:30.497 --> 00:02:31.472
Then you leave.

44
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.409
The team lead does the measuring alone.

45
00:02:35.112 --> 00:02:37.155
So there is no dependency on you.

46
00:02:38.205 --> 00:02:40.956
For client relationship and follow-up we often

47
00:02:41.014 --> 00:02:43.650
use a client evaluation and a follow-up.

48
00:02:45.002 --> 00:02:46.151
It all connects.

49
00:02:46.858 --> 00:02:49.668
The result is proven, so the sponsor signs.

50
00:02:50.364 --> 00:02:53.998
The lesson is an action, and the client can carry on alone.

51
00:02:54.987 --> 00:02:57.681
The project is not only done but closed.

52
00:02:58.453 --> 00:03:01.738
Line 3 runs, and the line belongs to the team.

53
00:03:03.035 --> 00:03:04.718
This is the map of Projects.

54
00:03:05.403 --> 00:03:08.572
Close is the last station on the road of a project.

55
00:03:09.612 --> 00:03:12.550
Close has four topics, each with four levels.

56
00:03:13.576 --> 00:03:16.386
Start with Proving results, at Basics level.

57
00:03:17.383 --> 00:03:21.516
At Working knowledge you read a run chart and close out the paperwork.

58
00:03:22.358 --> 00:03:25.052
Then come your own reflection and the follow-up.

59
00:03:26.071 --> 00:03:31.214
At Advanced you separate your own effect, stop early and design a retrospective.

60
00:03:31.967 --> 00:03:34.010
And you hold the client evaluation.

61
00:03:35.043 --> 00:03:37.319
At Expert you make a claim that holds.

62
00:03:38.039 --> 00:03:42.463
You hand over registers, make lessons travel and leave without dependency.

63
00:03:43.439 --> 00:03:47.526
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
